id: pm-w2krlt
title: "Historical GitHub artifact linkage: backfill canonical pm-item comments with resumable, rate-limit-aware evidence"
description: "Complete and continuously verify the repository-wide invariant that every GitHub issue and pull request has a public comment linking its canonical pm item. The 2026-08-04 audit found all 28 open issues compliant, then identified 468 historical closed artifacts without a PM-link comment before attempting a deterministic body-ID backfill. GitHub accepted a bounded subset and then returned a secondary content-creation rate limit; subsequent GraphQL census calls were intermittently unavailable with unexpected EOF. This item owns a resumable archive census, canonical-ID reconstruction for artifacts whose bodies contain no live PM ID, write pacing, verification, and a recurrence gate."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-04T09:16:47.188Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-04T09:22:18.406Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "A read-only full census reports every GitHub issue and pull request and the exact comment-linked count.; Every artifact has a verified comment linking a live canonical pm item; ambiguous historical artifacts have documented manual mapping decisions.; Backfill is resumable and idempotent, uses conservative pacing, and never reports an attempted comment as successful without read-back.; A regression check detects newly created GitHub artifacts without a PM link comment."
why_now: "The open backlog is compliant, but historical GitHub discussion still cannot reconstruct canonical PM lineage and bulk repair is constrained by GitHub secondary write throttling."
