comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-04T09:18:03.576Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-04: searched every PM status for historical GitHub issue and pull-request PM-link comments, artifact linkage backfill, and secondary content-creation rate limits. Existing roadmap, release, and quality items contain point-in-time open-artifact censuses, but no active or terminal item owns complete archive-wide verified comment linkage, ambiguous-ID reconstruction, paced writes, and recurrence detection. Initial census was 892 artifacts with 424 linked and 468 missing; all missing artifacts were closed. A deterministic body-ID backfill was attempted only for resolvable IDs, accepted a bounded subset, then GitHub returned a secondary content-creation limit. Read-back is required before the remaining count is trusted."
  "2026-08-04T09:22:18.406Z","harness:codex","Verified checkpoint 2026-08-04: 119 PM-link comments were read back from GitHub during this audit window. Six are the newly mapped open issues 885, 887, 888, 889, 890, and 891; 113 are historical closed artifacts accepted before secondary throttling. Starting from the post-open-intake census of 424 linked out of 892, the verified archive state is therefore 537 linked and 355 remaining. The remaining set must be re-censused and processed conservatively; no attempted parallel write is counted without read-back."
body: "Outcome: every issue and pull request has at least one verified comment containing a live .agents/pm/issues/pm-*.toon link. Preserve existing comments and immutable artifact history. Use read-only census first, derive links from valid body PM IDs where possible, manually resolve the remaining no-ID or retired-ID artifacts, write at a conservative bounded rate, and re-census after each checkpoint. Never treat attempted writes as success. Record GitHub rate-limit receipts and exact remaining artifact numbers."
